<%#
  One message in the generation log stream.  Rendered by
  Message#broadcast_message_to_generation_request (#13) via Turbo Stream append
  to #generation_log_<id> on the show page, and replayed there on revisit.

  Every agent turn — assistant prose, tool calls, and sandbox (tool) results —
  flows through one Markdown pipeline (MarkdownHelper#markdown_log_entry) so the
  log shares a single look: prose in Jost, code fences as Rouge-highlighted
  blocks (DESIGN.md, the Mono-Is-Machine Rule's prose exception).  log-entry-in
  animates the reveal.

  message.role: :assistant (LLM turn) | :tool (sandbox trial-run result) | :user
%>
<div id="<%= dom_id(message) %>" class="log-entry-in border border-edge-default bg-surface-raised p-3" data-role="<%= message.role %>">
  <p class="mb-1.5 font-mono text-xs text-content-muted"><%= message.role %></p>
  <div class="log-prose"><%= markdown_log_entry(message) %></div>
</div>
